		(property "ViaEvidence" "v0.9.9: User corrects raw battery+ versus post-Q1 rail. BATP -> Q1.S (single physical pad/native3, candidate drain); Q1.L/native2 (candidate source) -> U5.4/V011-V014. These are distinct copper nets, connected through Q1. TP14/R43.2/V015 is OUTA/H_MOTOR_A, supported by TP14-U5.8 = 1.5 ohm; the earlier battery-side photo interpretation is withdrawn. Q1.R/native1 is candidate gate at R44.2. Photo S means SINGLE, not MOSFET source."
			(at 96.52 100.33 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
			)
		)
		(property "IdentityEvidence" "R1A marking matches Formosa FMOS3401A datasheet p5; SOT-23 PMOS with G=1 (photo R), S=2 (photo L), D=3 (photo single S). Candidate identification, not manufacturer proof. Drain at battery+ and source at load support reverse-polarity protection; gate-control behavior not verified. Earlier MMBT3904 NPN hypothesis withdrawn."
			(at 96.52 100.33 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
			)
		)
		(property "CurrentEvidence" "TP14/U5.8 is OUTA, distinct from BATTERY+. Q1.R is the candidate MOSFET gate joined only to R44.2. R44 = 15 kohm (B83); OUTA-to-Q1.R rechecks = 21.4/21.7 kohm (B84/B85). These do not reproduce B61 = 516 ohm and are compatible with R44 in the path. Candidate identity, pin roles and powered behavior remain unverified. No wiring change inferred."
			(at 96.52 100.33 0)
